From: rhodep port <none@example.com>
Date: Tue, 19 Aug 2026 03:14:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: rhodep: add the rear camera

Enable CAMSS, CCI0 and the rear main camera: a Samsung S5KJN1 50 MP
sensor, which mainline already has a driver for.

Wiring comes from the vendor overlay
(blair-camera-sensor-mot-rhodep-overlay.dtsi): CCI0 master 1, CSIPHY0,
MCLK1 on gpio30 at 24 MHz, reset on gpio35, and the three rails supplied
by the FAN53870 camera PMIC added earlier. Four DPHY data lanes at
700 MHz, which is the only link frequency the driver offers.

Note the CCI pinctrl covers four pins, not two: each CCI master has its
own pin pair (gpio39/40 for master 0, gpio41/42 for master 1, per the
vendor's cci0_active and cci1_active). Declaring only one pair leaves the
other master electrically dead and the sensor never ACKs, which presents
as "i2c-qcom-cci: master 1 queue 0 timeout".

The other three sensors on this board (OV16A1Q, S5K4H7, GC02M1) sit on
CCI0 master 0 and have no mainline drivers, so they are not described.

Signed-off-by: rhodep port <none@example.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
@@ -1534,6 +1534,36 @@
 };
 
 &tlmm {
+	/*
+	 * CCI0 has two masters and each one has its own pin pair:
+	 * master 0 on gpio39/40 and master 1 on gpio41/42 (vendor
+	 * blair-pinctrl.dtsi, cci0_active and cci1_active). Declaring only
+	 * one pair leaves the other master electrically dead, which shows up
+	 * as "master 1 queue 0 timeout" and a sensor that never ACKs.
+	 */
+	cci0_default: cci0-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio39", "gpio40", "gpio41", "gpio42";
+		function = "cci_i2c";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-disable;
+	};
+
+	cam_rear_default: cam-rear-default-state {
+		mclk-pins {
+			pins = "gpio30";
+			function = "cam_mclk";
+			drive-strength = <4>;
+			bias-disable;
+		};
+
+		reset-pins {
+			pins = "gpio35";
+			function = "gpio";
+			drive-strength = <2>;
+			bias-disable;
+		};
+	};
+
 	cam_pmic_en_default: cam-pmic-en-default-state {
 		pins = "gpio33";
 		function = "gpio";
@@ -1548,3 +1578,55 @@
 		bias-pull-up;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Rear main camera: Samsung S5KJN1 (50 MP), on CCI0 master 1, CSIPHY0.
+ * Wiring from the vendor overlay (blair-camera-sensor-mot-rhodep-overlay.dtsi):
+ * MCLK1 on gpio30, reset on gpio35, and the three rails off the FAN53870.
+ */
+&cci0 {
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&cci0_default>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&cci0_i2c1 {
+	camera_rear: camera@10 {
+		compatible = "samsung,s5kjn1";
+		reg = <0x10>;
+
+		clocks = <&gcc GCC_CAMSS_MCLK1_CLK>;
+		assigned-clocks = <&gcc GCC_CAMSS_MCLK1_CLK>;
+		assigned-clock-rates = <24000000>;
+
+		vdda-supply = <&cam_vana>;
+		vddd-supply = <&cam_vdig>;
+		vddio-supply = <&cam_vio>;
+
+		reset-gpios = <&tlmm 35 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&cam_rear_default>;
+
+		port {
+			camera_rear_ep: endpoint {
+				data-lanes = <1 2 3 4>;
+				link-frequencies = /bits/ 64 <700000000>;
+				remote-endpoint = <&csiphy0_ep>;
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&camss {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	ports {
+		port@0 {
+			reg = <0>;
+			csiphy0_ep: endpoint {
+				data-lanes = <0 1 2 3>;
+				remote-endpoint = <&camera_rear_ep>;
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
